  "_solidFromOccluder": "Objects whose collider should be their full painted silhouette rather than the shape drawn in the colliders group. For a solid volume you can never enter, the two are the same thing, and tracing it twice only invites them to disagree. The fountain is here because its collider ellipse sat ~20px inside the painted stone rim, leaving a lip the player could stand on.",
  "solidFromOccluder": ["fountain"],

  "_banded": "Objects the player walks AROUND, which need one ground line per horizontal band instead of one for the whole shape. A wide base means the bottom edge is at a different depth at every x. Do NOT band a lamp or anything else whose head overhangs floor you can stand on — see slices() in import_traces.py.",
  "banded": ["fountain"],

